{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Sound the shofar on the new moon</b> — at the beginning of the moon's renewal, like: \"your new moons and your appointed seasons\" (Isaiah 1:14), new moon and Sabbath. And the blowing of trumpets is written in the Torah, and it is fitting that they would also blow on shofars. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted it regarding the day of Rosh HaShanah." "<b>And the meaning of בכסה</b> — that the moon is covered on it. And indeed this is the rule for every new moon." "<b>And the word חגינו</b> — the slaughter of the lambs, like: \"feasts shall pass\" (Lamentations?), \"bind the festival with cords\" (Psalm 118:27). And in my opinion: the word כסה is like a fixed time or a known appointed season, and thus: \"on the day of כסא he comes to his house\" (Daniel 1:14)."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 81, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:42.040625576Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}